  "worked_solution": "A function $f(x)$ is concave up on an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{\u2033}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nEarlier, we found that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2033}(x) & =-6x-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find where the function is concave up, we solve the inequality ${f}^{\u2033}(x)>0,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6x-6 & >0 \\\\ -6x & >6 \\\\ x & <-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is concave up on $(-\\infty ,-1)$",
